<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="Camunda MCP KB" id="id-93c87f2a1c5c42af98516913f8a2221f" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-20addffed8ec41fb8deb5a26bd2896e7" type="strategy"/>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-20732a98a98e4385a52f8bc9a9c4a377" type="business">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Team Member " id="id-83377bb290f6471d98855eadc5eae15b">
      <documentation>Anyone on the team who has content to contribute — no code changes needed.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Drop file into docs/knowledge-base/ " id="id-51a6f96acaaa429886ae572748496da8">
      <documentation>The entire manual step required. Any supported format, no naming convention or command to run.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Request: &quot;Add a payment retry gateway&quot; " id="id-19452bd1032f4f4f96eeef3498494dd4">
      <documentation>A concrete, real example ask — any natural-language request to build or modify a diagram.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Application" id="id-7666b5284ee54ab787762d90f46a770d" type="application">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Camunda-MCP Plugin  " id="id-84d32aa009284c198b3743bdea1e924b">
      <documentation>Camunda Desktop Modeler plugin exposing BPMN modeling + knowledge-base tools over MCP.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="MCP Server " id="id-5e369d3f780f4b819be34ffb412b9b38">
      <documentation>Existing. src/server.ts — the JSON-RPC/HTTP endpoint (POST /mcp). Registers all tools and resources per request.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Renderer Dispatch (bpmn-js) " id="id-213791cdbb4e4ee9b10ded1f78a7d942">
      <documentation>Existing. client/bpmn-tools.ts's TOOL_HANDLERS. The final stage — actually executes the validated, routed call against the live diagram via bpmn-js.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="KB Registry " id="id-17b8741f9b4c4e808b9ce15bde9a7bf5">
      <documentation>New. src/resources/registry.ts — serves hand-curated Markdown guides over MCP's native Resources protocol.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="KB Search Engine " id="id-8437523405d34ec18328d36fd32fbc34">
      <documentation>New. src/knowledge-base/* — SQLite FTS5 keyword search over an ingested, multi-format doc corpus (Markdown, PDF, BPMN XML, OCR'd images).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="MCP Client (Team's AI Agent)  " id="id-fd19a295c7f045f6845383435188c2d4">
      <documentation>Any MCP-compliant client (e.g. a teammate's Claude Code session) connecting to the plugin's MCP server.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="MCP Protocol Endpoint " id="id-ff1adb5d6e804b7c82fbde7e36e308a4">
      <documentation>The POST /mcp JSON-RPC endpoint — tools/call, resources/list, resources/read.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="BPMN Modeling Tools " id="id-2452fad6bb1f42689ecae3e0517ecd36">
      <documentation>manage_diagram, add_element, connect, layout, build_process, etc.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Guide Resources " id="id-2c48f415d9d04d6d91eb30b7b497f7e4">
      <documentation>resources/list + resources/read — curated Markdown guides (e.g. BPMN-BEST-PRACTICES.md).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="kb_search Tool " id="id-f22182e32585481994a0b61f122b0f7d">
      <documentation>Full-text keyword search over the knowledge base's indexed content — everything ingested from docs/knowledge-base/ (Markdown guides, PDFs, BPMN XML files, and OCR'd diagram images), chunked into the SQLite FTS5 index.

Given a query string, ranks matches using BM25: a relevance-scoring algorithm that weighs how often a search term appears in a document AND how distinctive that term is across the whole corpus, so a rare, specific word counts for more than a common one that appears everywhere. It's the same ranking family real search engines use — not a raw word-count match, and not semantic/AI similarity (no embeddings involved here, see the Context notes on Search Index).

Returns the top-N results as cited, highlighted excerpts — {title, sourceFile, sourceFormat, snippet} — not full documents, so an agent sees exactly which file matched and why, without needing a separate fetch for the common case.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Open BPMN Diagram " id="id-3547ade98e7c405fb35d93ccaa47b9a1">
      <documentation>The live diagram state inside the running Camunda Desktop Modeler.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="BPMN-BEST-PRACTICES.md " id="id-bf8fdb3d101c43ccb0af447108592539">
      <documentation>Existing repo-root file, read live off disk — no content duplication.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Search Index (SQLite FTS5) " id="id-f36bcce680cc42939dadf879a3f10fb6">
      <documentation>SQLite: a lightweight, embedded database engine — not a separate server, just a single file on disk, read and written directly by the plugin process. Zero setup, zero external service, zero network calls or cost per query.

FTS5: SQLite's built-in Full-Text Search extension. It builds a keyword index (word -> which rows contain it) and ranks results with BM25 (the same relevance-ranking family real search engines use). This is classic keyword search, not a vector/embeddings store — there is no AI model inference step, which is exactly why indexing stays fast regardless of corpus size at this scale (contrast: embedding-based search requires a model-inference call per chunk, which is the slow part in embedding pipelines like pgvector).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Reindex (manifest diff) " id="id-bd3f8bd165fd4ca3929d51a9840cdd9b">
      <documentation>src/knowledge-base/reindex.ts. Compares mtime/hash per source file against the last-indexed state and re-runs ingestion only for files that changed. One shared function, called from two independent triggers: the live file watcher and the plugin-load check.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Markdown Extractor (.md)  " id="id-208bc64ab6314666ad49e46d734196a0">
      <documentation>No package. Markdown is already plain text, so the file's content is used as-is — no parsing step needed.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="PDF Extractor (.pdf) " id="id-ff560843c93f4465b17579a9e34ffc9b">
      <documentation>Package: pdfjs-dist (Mozilla's own PDF.js, actively released, zero native dependencies). Extracts the PDF's text layer — works for anything with real text, not a scanned-only image.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="BPMN XML Extractor (.bpmn/.xml)  " id="id-1fcfec49e69a418bb4271a6c0e37edda">
      <documentation>No package. Built directly with simple, targeted extraction (element name attributes and &lt;documentation> tags) — BPMN XML's structure is small and predictable enough that a full XML parsing library isn't needed.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Image OCR Extractor (.png/.jpg) " id="id-94fc48bbf08641b9baf217472a76a759">
      <documentation>Package: tesseract.js (actively maintained, pure WebAssembly build of the Tesseract OCR engine). Fully local, no external API calls. Recovers visible text labels only — no understanding of the diagram's structure or meaning (see Future Considerations: a vision-model description path would give that, deferred pending real feedback).</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="KB File Watcher (chokidar) " id="id-033760238b454f07b5f7ea8b06ddc378">
      <documentation>New. Watches docs/knowledge-base/ live while the plugin is running (chokidar@4, debounced via awaitWriteFinish) and triggers the same reindex function the plugin-load check uses — no restart needed to pick up new content.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Live File Watcher (chokidar) " id="id-73995a55eb694fcea1f17568e1c8b2ab">
      <documentation>Watches docs/knowledge-base/ while the plugin is running. Debounced via chokidar's awaitWriteFinish so one save doesn't trigger several redundant reindex passes.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Plugin Load " id="id-835e2685073a43478b41d04d7e7e855d">
      <documentation>Fires once when the plugin/process itself loads (e.g. Modeler launches). Covers content that changed while the plugin wasn't running — e.g. pulled via git before launch.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="AI Agent (e.g. Claude Code)  " id="id-4dce1a468cfe4693b4f33488f1d957ae">
      <documentation>The MCP client driving the interaction — any MCP-compliant AI assistant connected to this plugin's MCP server.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="Format Extractors (by file type) " id="id-1d47971b74df40e28ea8c986c8bf2ff1">
      <documentation>src/knowledge-base/extractors/*. One small module per format — each takes a file path, returns extracted text. Reindex picks the right one by file extension.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Facade Routing " id="id-8721644586a945a7aef74b03d47d9956">
      <documentation>Existing. src/tools/handlers/facade.ts's resolveFacade(). Maps a public tool call (e.g. add_element {operation:&quot;task&quot;}) to its internal tool name (add_task). Runs first.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Tool Schemas (Zod) " id="id-fbe693d9dfb54f4ea633a63c54eb341a">
      <documentation>Existing. src/tools/schemas/{primitives,public}.ts + the SCHEMA_BY_TOOL lookup in handlers.ts. Validates params against the correct internal schema once the internal tool name is known.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Knowledge Base Database " id="id-b40b98b86d4040c39e8ce66c224e07c8">
      <documentation>knowledge-base.sqlite — generated at .data/, gitignored, never checked in. Fully regenerable from docs/knowledge-base/ via reindex(); a schema-version mismatch triggers a full drop-and-rebuild rather than an in-place migration.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="documents&#xA;&#xA;id INTEGER PK&#xA;title TEXT NOT NULL&#xA;source_file TEXT UNIQUE&#xA;source_format TEXT NOT NULL  &#xA;mtime_ms INTEGER NOT NULL &#xA;updated_at TEXT NOT NULL" id="id-4fbfe22b66224f73b60c7415d0417945">
      <documentation>id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT
title TEXT NOT NULL
source_file TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE
source_format TEXT NOT NULL
mtime_ms INTEGER NOT NULL
updated_at TEXT NOT NULL

One row per ingested file. mtime_ms is the manifest-diff column reindex() compares against disk to decide what changed.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="documents_fts&#xA;&#xA;title&#xA;body&#xA;rowid (= documents.id)  " id="id-fbea15ea877e4314859ce0f93efff1dc">
      <documentation>FTS5 virtual table (title, body)
rowid manually set to documents.id on insert

The actual searchable full-text index. bm25() ranking and snippet() excerpts run against this table; MATCH queries here, joined back to documents by rowid.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="schema_meta &#xA;&#xA;key TEXT PK&#xA;value TEXT" id="id-fd8fc6e018c2464f9ec4eadcafbb5bf1">
      <documentation>key TEXT PRIMARY KEY
value TEXT

Holds schema_version. On mismatch at startup, documents and documents_fts are dropped and rebuilt from scratch rather than migrated in place — safe because nothing here is irreplaceable.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
